From df3e7705141bf7f4629c116eda5e01eec4024814 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:49:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(state): futile FTS deferral keys on holder presence, not
 an identical PID set

The hub's stale index deferred 2,213 times over two days with foreign
holders present at every deferral, yet the record never turned futile:
the observed PID set changed every few deferrals (short-lived CLI holders,
and each process records its own view, which excludes itself), and any
change restarted the futility window. So the automatic online recovery
never ran and the index had to be repaired by hand.

The window now measures continuous presence of any foreign holder. It
restarts only when the record shows no deferral for longer than twice the
retry backoff cap (a new episode) or when the last deferral saw no holder.
Log and doctor text name the current holders instead of claiming the
same ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
